0..76 Comment "//! Dybjer and Setzer\'s signatures for inductive-recursive definitions, with"
77..149 Comment "//! the family a signature defines, its decoder and its eliminator, read"
150..171 Comment "//! through `std.ir`."
172..175 Comment "//!"
176..249 Comment "//! A signature describes a family and its decoder at once. It asks for a"
250..325 Comment "//! value of a type, for values of the family, or for a stop. The values of"
326..395 Comment "//! the family come through their decodes. A stop names one decode. A"
396..467 Comment "//! function computes the type of these arguments from the signature. A"
468..532 Comment "//! family and its decoder thus follow from the signature alone."
533..536 Comment "//!"
537..614 Comment "//! The signatures are a large type. A field of a signature holds a type. The"
615..687 Comment "//! pairs are data, and `args` returns them as terms by recursion on the"
688..764 Comment "//! signature. The family a signature defines is `IR(d, c)`, and its decoder"
765..838 Comment "//! is `el(d, c, m)`. Its one constructor `Intro` holds the arguments the"
839..914 Comment "//! signature asks for over the family itself. The pathological twin\'s `Mu`"
915..991 Comment "//! and `decodeMu` write the same pair as ordinary source, and stay refused."
992..1067 Comment "//! `elim` folds the family of an open signature. At `Intro(x)` the fold is"
1068..1133 Comment "//! the step at `x` and the fold mapped over `x`, by reflexivity."
1134..1137 Comment "//!"
1138..1217 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the family a code defines"
1218..1282 Comment "//!   and its decoder, refused, over the decode of its arguments"
1283..1360 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/universe/ir-eliminator.gandr` — an eliminator that"
1361..1405 Comment "//!   calls itself on its own value, refused"
1406..1485 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1999-finite_axiomatization_inductiverecursive_definitions]"
1486..1489 Comment "//!"
1490..1682 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1999-finite_axiomatization_inductiverecursive_definitions]: https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-48959-2_11 \"Dybjer and Setzer, A finite axiomatization of inductive-recursive definitions\""
1684..1755 Comment "// The signatures, their arguments, the family a signature defines, its"
1756..1786 Comment "// decoder and its eliminator."
